    "reading_order": 7,
    "text": "Do you remember what did the proof consist of ? It consisted of a sequence of\nstatements (called valid arguments), each following from the earlier statements in\nthe proof, or from previously proved (and known) results independent from the result\nto be proved, or from axioms, or from definitions, or from the assumptions you had\nmade. And you concluded your proof with the statement PQ = PR, i.e., the statement\nyou wanted to prove. This is the way any proof is constructed.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
    "confidence": 1.0
  },
  {
    "document_id": "NCERT_X_MATH_JEMH1A1",
    "page": 8,
